OpenLiteSpeed 1.9.3 — `noRemoteFetch 1`: no release check, no QUIC.cloud download.

On its first timer tick and every 30 minutes after, the server (process 1)
  - GETs https://openlitespeed.org/packages/release?ver=…&os=…&env=…&plat=…,
    reporting its version, OS and platform, and
  - downloads https://quic.cloud/ips?ln into $SERVER_ROOT/tmp/ and rewrites
    admin/conf/quic-cloud-ips.
Neither has a directive to turn it off. A local development server must work
offline and must not report on the person running it (measured 4 Oct 2026:
"HttpFetch: SSL Verify failed" in the log within a second of start).
`noRemoteFetch 1` at server level makes checkOLSUpdate(),
asyncDownloadQuicCloudTrustIp(), maybeDownloadQuicCloudTrustIp() and
downloadQuicCloudTrustIp() return before building a request. Default 0 keeps
upstream's behaviour. The static Cloudflare list (addCfTrustIp) is not a fetch
and is untouched.

The keyword is also registered in PlainConf's table (src/main/plainconf.cpp):
an unregistered server-level directive is logged "Not support [...]" and DROPPED,
so without that line the directive parses, does nothing, and the fetches still
fire — which is exactly what the build gate caught on its first run.

